{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/220337-recomended-trick-ammo","id":220337,"title":"Recomended \"trick\" ammo?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-06T10:57:13-07:00","id":220337,"title":"Recomended \"trick\" ammo?","content":"I'm a bit new to making a gun heavy character and I'm currently trying to make one that hunts a pretty wide variety of monsters. I'm currently planning on using silver, wrought iron, and blessed ammunition, but I know that a lot of targets are vulnerable to fire and the bullet options for causing that have various problems (tracer ammo doesn't burn strong enough, flares are inaccurate, dragon's breath will likely burn down the whole building on accident, etc.). I was wondering what seasoned hunters have done to overcome the problems with trying to apply ranged fire damage in a modern setting?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, other than silver, iron, fire, and blessed, I was wondering if there is another type of substance that is recommended for a all purpose monster hunter to carry in their back pocket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T23:49:20-07:00","id":220791,"title":"","content":"The best ammunition a hunter can have is information and surprise. That being said, it depends on the firarm you've specialized in. Shotguns, take a slug. Pistols, go for the biggest caliber you can. Rifle, aim for range and a .50 sniper rifle. These are all as subtle as a brick to the jaw, but they'll hurt anything they connect with. Actual trick ammo, in my experience, is rarely worth the effort to construct, however, a hand load of salt will help with shotgun crowd control.<br /> <br /> Fire is meant to be tricky to apply, so often your best bet is either prep ahead of time or accept collateral damage as par for the course. Hot coals should count as fire damage, and on the plus side you can fill a bucket with them. You could, in theory, weaponize something like a barbeque grill using a CO2 tank and cause it to spray the heated coals like a giant shotgun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T06:43:46-07:00","id":225037,"title":"","content":"One character I knew used homemade napalm and thermite not so much for actually killing things, but to bring attention to places. One of the best weapons of a Hunter, and one that 99% of Vampire, Mage, and Werewolf communities acknowledge as the trump card is Attention.<br /> <br /> If you burn a 2'-wide hole straight down through 6 stories of a building while the rooftop burns, it's doubtful you'll kill anything. However, everything inside is going to have a hell of a time getting their people/tools/monsters out while firetrucks and the bomb squad are racing to the scene. Doubly so if you call in the news teams. Best of all, it's a one-man operation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T23:13:43-07:00","id":225691,"title":"","content":"What about a flamethrower or assault rifle with underslung grenade launcher and phosphorus grenades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3447-sharkbone","name":"sharkbone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T08:44:31-07:00","id":226000,"title":"","content":"Acquiring one of those will get you looked at, and arrested by, the cops before you can even go out and hunt. There is no legal way of getting grenades, launchers or flamethrowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T08:51:13-07:00","id":226002,"title":"","content":"Of course not. But Hunters do it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3447-sharkbone","name":"sharkbone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T10:23:42-07:00","id":228170,"title":"","content":"Some interesting ideas here. My character does not yet have access to much of the major military grade hardware you mentioned (no grenade launchers or flamethrower). He's also more of a dextrous character than a strength based one so I don't think he could have those items very effectively at any rate, not to mention the legal issues...<br /> <br /> Grenades <i>are</i> something he can get his hands on though and I really like the idea of using those items to call attention to a monster's base of operations and make life much more difficult for it. Maybe doing something like that would open it up for an easier assassination attempt while it is mid-flight from it's recently evacuated home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}